Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: reject HFI-v3 encoder capture pool growth while streaming

HFI-v3 encoder output buffers are registered before resources are loaded.
CREATE_BUFS after STREAMON otherwise adds an unregistered address to the
capture queue, crashing MSM8996 VIDEO.VE.4.4-00060 in vbuffer.c:1219.
Registering that address during streaming is rejected by the firmware with
HFI_ERR_SESSION_INCORRECT_STATE (0x1006), so refuse late capture allocation
with EBUSY rather than submit an address the firmware cannot accept.

Initial allocation and capture allocation while stopped remain available;
the input queue and dynamic-buffer generations are unchanged. Applications
can allocate their full capture pool before STREAMON. GStreamer handles an
allocation refusal by copying retained compressed output and recycling the
existing buffers; encoding still uses Venus hardware.

Local hardware diagnosis; not submitted upstream.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -1098,6 +1098,15 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	if (*num_planes) {
+		/*
+		 * HFI v3 accepts static capture-buffer registration only before
+		 * the session starts. Do not let CREATE_BUFS introduce an
+		 * unregistered address while that session is streaming.
+		 */
+		if (IS_V3(core) && inst->streamon_cap &&
+		    q->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE)
+			return -EBUSY;
+
 		if (q->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE &&
 		    *num_planes != inst->fmt_out->num_planes)
 			return -EINVAL;
